                sections: [
                    AwakeningSection(heading: "Deprogramming ≠ Destroying Faith", body: "Here's what this module is NOT saying:\n\n• It's NOT saying God doesn't exist\n• It's NOT saying spiritual experience is fake\n• It's NOT saying every religious person is brainwashed\n• It's NOT saying you should hate your upbringing or your family\n• It's NOT saying churches/mosques/temples have zero value\n\nHere's what it IS saying:\n\nThere is a DIFFERENCE between genuine spiritual experience and institutionally programmed behavior. And most people have never separated the two because the programming was installed before they could tell the difference.\n\nGenuine spiritual experience:\n• Arises from within, not from external authority\n• Expands your sense of connection and freedom\n• Doesn't require guilt, fear, or threats to sustain itself\n• Survives questioning — in fact, DEEPENS through questioning\n• Empowers you to trust your own discernment\n• Doesn't need an institution to mediate your relationship with the source\n\nReligious programming:\n• Installed from outside, during suggestible developmental windows\n• Constrains behavior through guilt, fear, and social pressure\n• Requires repetition to maintain (miss church for a few months and the hold weakens — that's a sign it's programming, not truth)\n• Punishes questioning\n• Creates dependency on mediators between you and the divine\n• Needs an institution to survive\n\nThe goal isn't to become an atheist. The goal is to run a CLEAN INSTALL.\n\nKeep what's genuine. Delete what was installed without your consent. And going forward, choose — CONSCIOUSLY choose — what runs on your operating system.\n\nThat's the difference between faith and programming. Faith is chosen. Programming is inflicted."),
                    AwakeningSection(heading: "The Deprogramming Protocol", body: "A practical framework for separating signal from code:\n\nSTEP 1: INVENTORY\nWrite down every religious belief you hold. Every practice. Every fear. Every guilt trigger. Every ritual you perform or avoid.\n\nNow mark each one: Did I CHOOSE this as an adult with full information? Or was it INSTALLED before I could evaluate it?\n\nBe honest. Most of what you'll find was installed.\n\nSTEP 2: TRACE THE SOURCE\nFor each installed belief, ask: WHO installed this? WHEN? WHAT was the method? (Repetition? Fear? Authority? Social pressure? Ritual?)\n\nThis isn't about blame. Your parents were programmed too. Their parents were programmed. The chain goes back centuries. You're not looking for villains — you're looking for the MECHANISM so you can disarm it.\n\nSTEP 3: TEST IN ISOLATION\nTake each belief and strip away the programming context. Ask: If I had never been told this, would I arrive at it independently through my own experience and reasoning?\n\n• \"I should treat others with compassion\" — you might arrive at this independently. Keep it.\n• \"I deserve eternal punishment for being human\" — you would NEVER arrive at this independently. It was installed. Flag it.\n• \"There is something greater than myself\" — many people arrive at this through direct experience. Keep it.\n• \"That something greater can only be accessed through one specific institution\" — you would never conclude this independently. Flag it.\n\nSTEP 4: FEEL THE RESISTANCE\nWhen you consider deleting a flagged belief, notice what happens in your body. Fear? Guilt? Anxiety? A feeling that something terrible will happen?\n\nThat's the programming's defense mechanism activating. The code was written to resist deletion. The fear you feel when questioning is NOT evidence that the belief is true. It's evidence that the programming is sophisticated.\n\nSit with the fear. Don't act on it. Don't retreat. Just observe it. Name it: \"This is the defense mechanism. This is the code protecting itself.\"\n\nIt passes. It always passes. Because it was never yours.\n\nSTEP 5: REBUILD BY CHOICE\nOnce you've cleared the installed code, you're standing in open space. This can feel terrifying — or exhilarating.\n\nNow you get to CHOOSE. For the first time. What do YOU believe? Not your parents. Not your priest. Not your culture. YOU.\n\nMaybe you choose some of the same beliefs — but now they're CHOSEN, not installed. That changes everything. A chosen belief is alive. An installed belief is a cage.\n\nMaybe you build something new. A personal framework drawn from every tradition, filtered through your own experience, tested against the Discernment Protocol (Module 5, Lesson 3).\n\nMaybe you find that the genuine spiritual signal — the real connection to something greater — was always there, buried under layers of institutional code. And with the code removed, the signal is actually CLEARER.\n\nThat's the paradox of deprogramming: removing the religious code often makes the spiritual experience MORE vivid, not less. Because the institution was never the source. The institution was the MIDDLEMAN. And middlemen always take a cut.\n\nYour connection to the source doesn't need a priest. It doesn't need a building. It doesn't need a calendar. It doesn't need ash on your forehead.\n\nIt just needs you. Awake. Aware. Choosing freely.\n\nThat's not apostasy. That's sovereignty.\n\nRun YOUR code. On YOUR operating system. By YOUR choice.\n\nThat's Aperture. Wide open. No permission required. 🌅"),
                ],
                reflectionPrompt: "If I ran the Inventory right now — how much of my spiritual life was CHOSEN vs. INSTALLED? Am I ready to start separating the two?"
